v0.9.9-beta1: AI Feed SSE, Webhook Bridge, Auto-Diagnostic, QuillonOS, 46 MCP tools

AI Feed - Real-time SSE + Polling:
- serve.rs: SSE loop polls /tmp/flux-events/ for cross-process events
- serve.rs: push_feed_event() writes feed_*.json for MCP-to-serve bridge
- serve.rs: /api/feed endpoint returns last 20 events as JSON
- serve.rs: /api/tune GET+POST endpoints, OPTIONS CORS preflight
- serve.rs: handle_build_event detects error reports for auto-diagnostic
- fluxc-mcp: push_feed_event called after every tool dispatch
- webhook.rs: auto_dispatch pushes AI feed events on webhook fire
- webhook.rs: test_webhook_url() for flux_webhook_test tool
- dashboard_sse.html: EventSource SSE + 3s polling fallback
- dashboard_sse.html: dynamic URLs (hostname), status dot, tune slider wired

QuillonOS Desktop Prototype:
- quillonos.html: 11-app desktop OS (Browser, Flux, Files, Terminal,
  SysMon, Wallet, Miner, DEX, IDE, Journal, Pro)
- Draggable/resizable windows, start menu with search, taskbar, system tray
- Interactive terminal with 15 commands (fluxc, mine, wallet, etc.)
- File explorer, system monitor, wallet UI, DEX, miner stats
- CheerpX Linux VM: dual-CDN fallback, init()/create() API detection
- Auto-error reporting: POSTs to /api/build_event on failures

Rust Wrapper Fix:
- main.rs: FLUXC_WRAPPING check changed to =="1" (was .is_ok())
- lib.rs: wrapper_mode graceful error instead of panic

MCP Tools: 44 to 46:
- flux_predict_batch: predict all 15 crates in 1 call
- flux_webhook_test: signed HMAC ping to verify endpoints
- flux_fullcheck: now includes predict_batch in health report

Systemd:
- fluxc-serve.service: removed stray FLUXC_WRAPPING=0
- Enabled with Restart=always, MemoryMax=256M

Version bump: v0.9.8-beta1 to v0.9.9-beta1
